Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 23:57:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Point the booking CTA at Google Calendar, site-wide

"Book a discovery call" -> "Book a call with Jerrell", now linking straight
to https://calendar.app.google/noDsozbsi8Y2pbUW7 instead of routing through
/contact. Twelve instances across every page: the nav (desktop and mobile),
the Home hero and closing band, the four pillar hero secondaries, About, the
Work hub, the case-study template and the blog-post template.

The URL and label live in content/site.json under `booking`, so the five
components that had the CTA hardcoded now read it from one place. Page JSONs
keep their own copies, matching how the rest of the copy in this repo works.
The four pillar pages keep their trailing arrow.

Button renders an external href as a plain anchor rather than next/link,
with target="_blank" and rel="noopener noreferrer": next/link is for internal
navigation, the visitor should not lose the page they were reading to a
third-party booking form, and noopener denies that page a handle on this
window. Hero's secondary text link gets the same treatment. Both switch on
the href, so any future external CTA is handled correctly without a flag to
remember.

mockups/home.html still carries the old label. It is the approved visual
spec, a record of what was signed off, not shipped code.

Verified on a production build: all twelve routes render the booking link,
every one carries the correct URL with target and rel, no page still says
"Book a discovery call", and the only labels rendered are "Book a call with
Jerrell" and its arrow variant.

